content.text:
I found three real places for a preschooler. One caveat on the dates: today is October 12, 2026, so September 12 to 15, 2026 has already passed. If you mean next September, the hours and prices below are from the 2026 season and should be checked again.

```json
{
  "picks": [
    {
      "name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan (CMOM), 212 West 83rd Street",
      "age_fit": "children ages 0-6",
      "when": "Tuesday-Sunday, 10am-5pm on their main pages. Their visitor guidelines list July-September as open daily, so check Monday before going.",
      "source_name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan"
    },
    {
      "name": "Children's Zoo at the Bronx Zoo",
      "age_fit": "family attraction with prairie dogs, turtles, an anteater and a farmyard to pet and feed goats, sheep and alpacas",
      "when": "Children's Zoo 10:00-4:30 on weekdays, 10:00-5:00 on weekends. The zoo opens at 10am and grounds close at 5pm weekdays and 5:30pm weekends, April to October.",
      "source_name": "Bronx Zoo"
    },
    {
      "name": "New York Aquarium, Coney Island",
      "age_fit": "Child (3-12) tickets; children 2 and under free",
      "when": "Daily 10:00am-5:00pm, September 8 to October 31, 2026; last entry 4:00pm",
      "price": "Child (3-12) $25.95 off-peak or $27.95 peak; adult (13 and over) $29.95 or $32.95",
      "source_name": "New York Aquarium"
    }
  ]
}
```

- **CMOM:** I found no current price on their own pages, so none is listed.
- **Bronx Zoo:** Their pages gave no current ticket price either. The zoo's FAQ says the Children's Zoo is a seasonal attraction that closes from November through March.
- **New York Aquarium:** Their hours page shows the 2026 rates and hours. Their free Wednesday-afternoon admission needs advance timed tickets, which a Macaroni Kid listing says open the Monday before.

